From 88f1e7d287a3cac1ec1aac00fa17e5874a13a8ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A3 <a3@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 22:06:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1710/1712] pokeathlon: use the SDK width types at the
 course-object call sites

NitroSDK declares s32/fx32 as long, so under devkitARM 16.1 (GCC 14) the
course-object helpers no longer accept the game int locals and frame
fields without an incompatible-pointer-types error. Under SDK_PORT_3DS,
give those locals, struct fields and the two local prototypes in
pennant_capture_field.c the callee exact types (s32/fx32); the original
MWCC/DS declarations stay under #else.

Fixes the 3DS compile of src/pokeathlon/{circle_push,circle_push_field,
disc_catch,disc_catch_field,goal_roll,goal_roll_field,hurdle_dash_race,
lamp_jump,pennant_capture,pennant_capture_cpu,pennant_capture_field,
pennant_capture_play,relay_run,relay_run_cpu,ring_drop_field,
ring_drop_mon}.c and include/pokeathlon/{circle_push,relay_run_cpu}.h.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
